  "where": "Acceptance Criteria, the CR-12 / H5 PERCEPTION_OUT read-view AC (line 1022), clause (iii)",
  "issue": "The AC still says a PRESENTATION subscriber 'receives the populated view in both' profiles. The 2026-10-29 ADR-0003 sync (CR-12 text at line 136, PRESENTATION row at line 124, Overlay row at line 232) now says PresentationViews has two faces. Only a facet issued with perception_access (the Filter's and the DIAGNOSTIC facets) gets the real view. Every other PRESENTATION facet gets empty_view and counts PERCEPTION_READ_BLOCKED. An implementer who writes the test as stated would require a generic presentation subscriber to read perception data. That contradicts the rule and ADR-0003 section 7. The same AC says PERCEPTION_READ_BLOCKED increments by 2, which would now be wrong for a default-face reader.",
  "fix": "Split (iii). (iii-a): a PRESENTATION facet issued with perception_access (the Filter) receives the populated view. (iii-b): a default-face PRESENTATION facet receives empty_view, PERCEPTION_READ_BLOCKED increments, and a violation is recorded (both profiles). Update the count to 'by 3' with the three blocked readers, and mark it '(Amended 2026-10-29 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d sync knock-on fix, round 3)'."
